{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/shapleyattributions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/ShapleyAttributions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"SwiftExplain"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"SHAP & LIME Model Interpretability"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Explain machine learning model predictions with game-theoretic Shapley value attributions (TreeSHAP, KernelSHAP) and local linear surrogates (LIME)."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP","doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAPExplanation","doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/LIMEExplainer"],"title":"Explainability Engines","anchor":"Explainability-Engines"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/ModelInterpretability"],"title":"Guides & Tutorials","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain"]]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Black-box machine learning models—such as deep neural networks, random forests, and gradient boosting trees—produce accurate predictions but obscure the individual feature contributions that drove a particular decision.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftExplain","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" provides mathematically grounded, axiomatic interpretability algorithms:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Path-dependent Shapley attributions for "},{"code":"DecisionTreeClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"DecisionTreeRegressor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"RandomForestClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"RandomForestRegressor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"GradientBoostedTreesRegressor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Solves trees with "},{"code":"K <= TreeSHAP.maxExactFeatures","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"12","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") distinct split features exactly via $2^K$ coalition enumeration ("},{"code":"O(2^K · L)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per tree), and uses deterministic seeded Monte Carlo permutation sampling ("},{"code":"approximationSamples = 2048","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") with exact additive efficiency enforcement ($\\sum_i \\phi_i = f(x) - \\mathbb{E}[f(X)]$) for larger $K$. Supports both "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeNodeWeighting\/uniformLeaf","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (default) and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeNodeWeighting\/empiricalCover","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", as well as per-class probability decomposition."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Model-agnostic explainer solving constrained weighted linear regression against an empirical background dataset for any arbitrary asynchronous prediction function."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/LIMEExplainer","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations fitting ridge linear surrogate models around perturbed neighborhoods."}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"mermaid","code":["graph TD","    Model[Trained Model \/ Ensemble] --> ModelType{Model Architecture}","    ModelType -->|Tree Ensemble \/ Forest| Tree[TreeSHAP: Exact K<=12 \/ Seeded MC K>12]","    ModelType -->|Arbitrary Black-Box \/ Pipeline| Kernel[KernelSHAP: Empirical Regression]","    ModelType -->|Local Linear Surrogate| LIME[LIMEExplainer: Perturbation Neighborhood]","    Tree --> Attributions[Shapley Attributions: sum phi_i = f(x) - E(f)]","    Kernel --> Attributions","    LIME --> SurrogateWeights[Local Coefficients + R^2 Goodness of Fit]","    Attributions --> FeatureRanking[Feature Importance Ranking & Waterfall Breakdown]"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"1-Path-Dependent-TreeSHAP-for-Tree-Ensembles","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"1. Path-Dependent TreeSHAP for Tree Ensembles"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP","type":"reference"},{"text":" evaluates path-dependent conditional expectations over a tree’s internal sample weights (Lundberg et al., 2018; Nature Machine Intelligence):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a tree splits on "},{"code":"K <= TreeSHAP.maxExactFeatures","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"12","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") distinct features, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" enumerates all $2^K$ coalitions to return "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"exact"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" path-dependent Shapley values ("},{"code":"O(2^K · L)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per tree)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"code":"K > 12","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" switches to deterministic Monte Carlo permutation sampling ("},{"code":"TreeSHAP.approximationSamples = 2048","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"permutationSeed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), renormalizing any efficiency discrepancy evenly across active features. Use "},{"code":"treeShap.isExact(tree:numFeatures:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to inspect which regime a tree uses."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Leaf weighting defaults to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeNodeWeighting\/uniformLeaf","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"1.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per leaf) and can be configured to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeNodeWeighting\/empiricalCover","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" using "},{"code":"FlatTreeNode.cover","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (falling back to "},{"code":"1.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when decoding legacy "},{"code":"<= 3.13.3","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" serialized models without "},{"code":"cover","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For "},{"code":"GradientBoostedTreesRegressor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"explainDetailed(gbdt:instance:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"explain(gbdt:instance:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"explainBatch(gbdt:instances:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" decompose "},{"code":"initialPrediction + learningRate * sum_m T_m(x)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For "},{"code":"DecisionTreeClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"RandomForestClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"explainClassDetailed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"explainAllClassesDetailed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"explainBatchClass","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" decompose per-class ","type":"text"},{"code":"predictProbability","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" outputs (including ","type":"text"},{"code":"ForestProbabilityMode.hardVote","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ForestProbabilityMode.softLeafDistribution","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), while ","type":"text"},{"code":"explain(decisionTree:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"explain(randomForest:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" preserve scalar ","type":"text"},{"code":"FlatTreeNode.value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" semantics.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftML","import SwiftExplain","","\/\/ 1. Train a Random Forest model on feature data","let rf = RandomForestClassifier(nEstimators: 50, maxDepth: 6)","try await rf.fit(features: X_train, targets: y_train)","","\/\/ 2. Initialize TreeSHAP explainer","let treeShap = TreeSHAP()","","\/\/ 3. Compute exact Shapley attributions for an individual observation","let testInstance = X_test[0]","let shapValues = await treeShap.explain(randomForest: rf, instance: testInstance)","","\/\/ 4. Rank features by absolute impact on the decision","let featureNames = [\"Income\", \"DebtToIncome\", \"CreditScore\", \"EmploymentYears\", \"LoanAmount\"]","let ranked = zip(featureNames, shapValues).sorted { abs($0.1) > abs($1.1) }","","print(\"Feature attributions for instance:\")","for (name, phi) in ranked {","    let direction = phi >= 0 ? \"+\" : \"-\"","    print(\"  • \\(name): \\(direction)\\(String(format: \"%.4f\", abs(phi)))\")","}"]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Concurrent-Batch-Explanations","type":"heading","text":"Concurrent Batch Explanations"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For dataset-wide interpretability or global summary plots, compute attributions concurrently across Apple Silicon CPU cores:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let flatTrees = await rf.flatTrees","let batchAttributions = await treeShap.explainBatch(","    trees: flatTrees,","    instances: X_test,","    numFeatures: featureNames.count",")","print(\"Computed SHAP matrix for \\(batchAttributions.count) instances.\")"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"2-Model-Agnostic-Explanations-with-KernelSHAP","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"2. Model-Agnostic Explanations with `KernelSHAP`"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When interpreting models without tree structures—such as support vector machines, neural decoders, or multi-stage pipelines—"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" estimates Shapley values through weighted linear regression over coalition permutations:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftExplain","","\/\/ 1. Initialize KernelSHAP explainer actor","let kernelShap = KernelSHAP()","","\/\/ 2. Compute Shapley attributions using background baseline dataset","let attributions = await kernelShap.explain(","    model: { features in","        \/\/ Any asynchronous prediction function mapping [Double] -> Double","        return await myNeuralNetwork.predict(features)","    },","    instance: testInstance,","    background: backgroundSampleData,","    numCoalitions: 300",")","","print(\"KernelSHAP Attributions: \\(attributions)\")"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"3-Local-Surrogate-Explanations-with-LIME","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"3. Local Surrogate Explanations with LIME"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/LIMEExplainer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" perturbs the target instance with Gaussian noise, queries the black-box model on the neighborhood, and trains an interpretable, locally-weighted ridge linear surrogate:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftExplain","","let lime = LIMEExplainer(kernelWidth: 0.75, regularization: 1.0)","","let explanation = await lime.explain(","    model: { x in await complexPipeline.predictScore(x) },","    instance: testInstance,","    numSamples: 500",")","","print(\"Local Model Intercept: \\(explanation.intercept)\")","print(\"Local Surrogate Fidelity (R²): \\(String(format: \"%.3f\", explanation.localR2))\")","","for (idx, weight) in explanation.featureWeights.enumerated() {","    print(\"Feature \\(idx) Local Weight: \\(String(format: \"%.4f\", weight))\")","}"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/KernelSHAP":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KernelSHAP"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/kernelshap","title":"KernelSHAP","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model interpretation using the KernelSHAP algorithm."}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KernelSHAP","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/TreeSHAPExplanation":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TreeSHAPExplanation"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/treeshapexplanation","title":"TreeSHAPExplanation","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAPExplanation","abstract":[{"text":"Explanation structure containing TreeSHAP attributions and baseline predictions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(exact when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"K <= TreeSHAP.maxExactFeatures"},{"text":", seeded Monte Carlo permutation estimate otherwise).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TreeSHAPExplanation"}]},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain","title":"SwiftExplain","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model Explainability, SHAP & Feature Attributions."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/LIMEExplainer":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/LIMEExplainer","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations (LIME).","type":"text"}],"title":"LIMEExplainer","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/limeexplainer","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"LIMEExplainer","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LIMEExplainer"}]},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/TreeSHAP":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TreeSHAP"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/treeshap","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP","title":"TreeSHAP","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeSHAP (Tree Shapley Additive Explanations) for decision trees, random forests, and gradient boosted trees"},{"type":"text","tex